{
  "version": 1,
  "title": "The Last Seating of the Meridian Atomic",
  "summary": "In 1957 the Meridian Atomic Limited was sold as the future of travel, a streamlined dining car serving 'radiant cuisine' to paying guests. In truth, a government-funded lab was using the car to test an irradiated food additive on unsuspecting passengers, with a sealed reactor-cooled galley at the far end. The experiment went badly wrong during one dinner service: the diners and staff were changed and the car was quietly sealed off on a forgotten siding. The player pieces together the cover-up from the quarantine notices outside and the abandoned, glowing table settings, charts and galley equipment inside.",
